BT /F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 722 Tm (CHAPTER 1: Limits, Continuity, and Differentiation) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694 Tm (1.1 Limits and the Squeeze Theorem) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 674 Tm (A limit describes the value that a function $f\(x\)$ approaches as the input $x$ approaches $c$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 659 Tm (Continuity is defined as the property where $\\lim_{x \\to c} f\(x\) = f\(c\)$ holds at an interior point $c$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 644 Tm (Indeterminate Form: A limit ratio such as $\\frac{0}{0}$ whose limiting value requires algebraic simplification.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 620 Tm (THEOREM 1.1 The Squeeze Theorem) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 604 Tm (If $h\(x\) \\le f\(x\) \\le g\(x\)$ for all $x$ in an open interval containing $c$ except possibly at $c$ itself,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 589 Tm (and if $\\lim_{x \\to c} h\(x\) = L = \\lim_{x \\to c} g\(x\)$, then $\\lim_{x \\to c} f\(x\) = L$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 565 Tm (Special trigonometric limit: $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin x}{x} = 1$ underpins trigonometric differentiation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 539 Tm (1.2 Differentiation, Chain Rule, and Quotient Rule) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 519 Tm (The derivative of a function $f$ at $x$ is given by $f'\(x\) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f\(x + h\) - f\(x\)}{h}$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 504 Tm (The Quotient Rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}\\left[\\frac{f\(x\)}{g\(x\)}\\right] = \\frac{g\(x\)f'\(x\) - f\(x\)g'\(x\)}{[g\(x\)]^{2}}$) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 489 Tm (The Chain Rule states that if $y = f\(u\)$ and $u = g\(x\)$ are differentiable, then $\\frac{dy}{dx} = f'\(g\(x\)\)g'\(x\)$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 474 Tm (The derivative of $\\tan x$ is $\\sec^{2} x$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 459 Tm (The derivative of $\\ln x$ is $\\frac{1}{x}$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 444 Tm (When the derivative $f'\(x\)$ is positive on an open interval, the function $f$ increases across that interval.) Tj ET
endstream
