BT /F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 722 Tm (CHAPTER 2: Definite Integrals and Infinite Series) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694 Tm (2.1 Riemann Sums and the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 674 Tm (Riemann Sum is defined as a finite approximation $\\sum_{i=1}^{n} f\(c_{i}\)\\,\\Delta x_{i}$ over a partition of $[a, b]$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 659 Tm (Antiderivative refers to a differentiable function $F$ satisfying $F'\(x\) = f\(x\)$ across an interval.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 635 Tm (THEOREM 2.1 The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 619 Tm (If a function $f$ is continuous on the closed interval $[a, b]$ and $F$ is an antiderivative of $f$ on $[a, b]$,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 604 Tm (then $\\int_{a}^{b} f\(x\)\\,dx = F\(b\) - F\(a\)$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 580 Tm (Integration by Parts Formula: $\\int u\\,dv = uv - \\int v\\,du$) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 554 Tm (2.2 Convergence of Geometric and Taylor Series) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 534 Tm (Geometric Series: An infinite series $\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} ar^{n}$ with nonzero first term $a$ and common ratio $r$.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 510 Tm (THEOREM 2.2 Convergence of a Geometric Series) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 494 Tm (A geometric series with common ratio $r$ converges to the sum $\\frac{a}{1 - r}$ when $|r| < 1$,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 479 Tm (and the geometric series diverges whenever $|r| \\ge 1$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 457 Tm (Taylor Series refers to the power series representation $\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{f^{\(n\)}\(c\)}{n!}\(x - c\)^{n}$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 442 Tm (As the degree $n$ of a Taylor polynomial increases, the truncation remainder decreases near the center $c$.) Tj ET
endstream
