BT /F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 722 Tm (CHAPTER 3: Algorithms, Complexity, and Graph Theory) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 694 Tm (3.1 Asymptotic Complexity, Recurrences, and Divide-and-Conquer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 674 Tm (Asymptotic Complexity is defined as the growth rate of an algorithm running time $T\(n\)$ as input size $n \\to \\infty$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 659 Tm (Merge sort runs in $O\(n \\log n\)$ time in the worst case by recursively sorting two subarrays of size $n/2$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 644 Tm (The recurrence for merge sort is $T\(n\) = 2T\(n/2\) + O\(n\)$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 629 Tm (The running time of binary search is $O\(\\log n\)$.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 605 Tm (THEOREM 3.1 The Master Theorem) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 589 Tm (For a divide-and-conquer recurrence $T\(n\) = aT\(n/b\) + \\Theta\(n^{d}\)$ with constants $a \\ge 1$ and $b > 1$,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 86 574 Tm (if $d = \\log_{b} a$ then the asymptotic solution satisfies $T\(n\) = \\Theta\(n^{d} \\log n\)$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 552 Tm (Iterative binary search maintains midpoint $m = \\lfloor \(low + high\) / 2 \\rfloor$ and halves $[low, high]$.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 526 Tm (3.2 Graph Traversals and Shortest-Path Algorithms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 506 Tm (Directed Acyclic Graph: A directed graph with no directed cycles that admits a linear topological ordering.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 491 Tm (Binary Heap refers to a complete binary tree satisfying the heap-order property at every internal node.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 476 Tm (Dijkstra's algorithm runs in $O\(\(V + E\) \\log V\)$ time on weighted graphs with nonnegative edge weights.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 461 Tm (When graph edge density increases toward $V^{2}$, adjacency-matrix lookup latency decreases relative to lists.) Tj ET
endstream
